cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If claude-session-publisher helped you archive or cite an AI-assisted session, please cite it."
title: "claude-session-publisher: full-fidelity, citable archives of Claude Code sessions"
type: software
version: "2.7.6"
date-released: "2026-09-04"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/fabiocampolim-design/claude-session-publisher"
authors:
  - family-names: Campolim
    given-names: Fabio
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - research transparency
  - AI-assisted research
  - transcripts
  - archiving
  - Claude Code
  - LaTeX
  - provenance
abstract: >-
  Standard-library Python tool that turns a Claude Code, Claude Desktop cowork
  or claude.ai session into a single self-contained document in HTML, plain
  text, Markdown, LaTeX or PDF. Every source record is rendered, folded into an
  earlier turn, or counted as deliberately not rendered, and the three are
  reconciled against the source record count in a fidelity report on the page,
  so the difference between "not in the transcript" and "not in the source" is
  always visible. Human turns stay verbatim, prompts and responses carry
  sequential P/R reference tags a paper can cite, resumed sessions are chain
  resolved by record-uuid comparison, and usage is deduped per request id and
  priced beside Claude Code's own reported cost meter.
